# Azure Deployment Plan: FlowDesk

## Goal

FlowDesk is deployed as a temporary, student-budget-aware Azure demo using Azure CLI and direct Node.js deployment to a Linux App Service Free (F1) plan.

## Project information

- **Application:** FlowDesk
- **Runtime:** Node.js 22
- **Application stack:** TypeScript, Express, plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript
- **Listening port:** 3000 (`PORT`)
- **Health endpoint:** `GET /api/health`
- **Readiness endpoint:** `GET /api/readyz`
- **Operational logs:** JSON request summaries on stdout; request IDs returned as `X-Request-Id`
- **Data:** In-memory demo data; it resets on restart and is not suitable for persistent production use.
- **Authentication:** Demo credentials and a fixed demo token are present and displayed on the sign-in page. This public app is only for a temporary, non-sensitive demo.
- **Authorization:** Admin, Manager, Member, and Viewer demo roles are enforced server-side with project-scoped reads and mutations; the deployed update was verified against all four roles.
- **Container:** A Node.js 22 Dockerfile is present but is not part of the selected deployment; Docker is not installed locally.
- **Target host:** Azure App Service on Linux, Free (F1), Indonesia Central, in resource group `rg-flowdesk-demo`.

## Deployed architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
  user["Browser"] --> app["FlowDesk: Azure App Service Linux (F1) in Indonesia Central"]
```

FlowDesk is currently self-contained and uses in-memory sample data. The temporary demo intentionally avoids a database, container registry, Application Insights, and Log Analytics to limit setup and potential charges. Use JSON stdout request logs and health endpoints for basic validation. Demo credentials are public and data resets on restart; never use the demo for sensitive data.

## Deployed Azure resources

| Resource | Purpose | Sizing / configuration |
|---|---|---|
| Linux App Service Plan | Hosts the web app | `asp-flowdesk-demo`, Free (F1), Indonesia Central. |
| Linux Web App | Runs FlowDesk | `flowdesk-demo-399203`, Node.js 22 LTS, HTTPS-only, port 3000, direct code deployment without a custom container. |

## Applied configuration

- `PORT=3000`
- No additional secrets are needed for this temporary demo.
- HTTPS-only access is enabled; `/api/readyz` has been verified.
- Frontend and API are served from the same origin; cross-origin access is not required.

